{#
    Captcha Refresh Form -- the POST target for the "new code" button

    An empty form carrying only its CSRF token, so the button inside the captcha fieldset can
    reach it through the HTML `form` attribute. It must sit outside the page's own form, since
    nesting one form in another is invalid markup and the browser drops the inner one. Include
    it once per page that renders _components/human_check.html.twig, after that page's
    form_end(). With JavaScript on, captcha-counter.js intercepts the button and swaps the
    image in place instead, so the visitor keeps what they already typed.

    Used in:    templates/security/register.html.twig, templates/security/reset.html.twig,
                templates/support/index.html.twig
    Parameters:
        - form (FormView, required)   -- the meta child of that page's form
#}
{% if form.captcha is defined %}
    <form id="captchaRefresh" method="post" action="{{ path('app_captcha_refresh', {'context': form.vars.context}) }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('captcha_refresh' ~ form.vars.context) }}">
    </form>
{% endif %}
